{
  "about": "QO8 side-by-side WinISD/openisd parity scenarios. Every scenario is stated in EXPLICIT VALUES and names no driver from the database — a fixture that said 'Dayton RS180-8' would silently re-baseline itself the next time the scraper pipeline regenerated that record. Keys are WinISD's own .wdr/.wpr key names, so the generator writes them straight into a project file and the goldens read back in the same vocabulary. See README.md for the method, the WinISD build, the refresh command and what every parameter means.",
  "driverKeysAreEnteredValues": "Only the keys listed under `driver` are written to the project file. Everything else is left ABSENT so WinISD's own consistency solver decides it — which is the thing under test. A scenario that lists Qts, Cms, Mms, Rms, BL and Vas leaves the solver nothing to do and tests the derived/advanced pass alone.",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "sealed-small",
      "purpose": "Sealed alignment, 20 L. Box.Fr is WinISD's computed sealed system resonance Fsc at full precision, so this scenario carries a box-side row as well as the driver-side ones.",
      "driver": {
        "Brand": "QO8", "Model": "sealed-small",
        "Znom": 8, "Pe": 100, "SPL": 90, "Le": 0.0005, "numVC": 1, "VCCon": 2,
        "Hc": 0, "Hg": 0, "Xmax": 0.006,
        "Fs": 37.2, "Mms": 0.0155, "Cms": 0.0011809260025671645, "Re": 6.4,
        "Qms": 3.8, "BL": 7.5, "Sd": 0.0132, "Qes": 0.41220376440829154,
        "Qts": 0.3718657482780974, "Rms": 0.9533906968736183,
        "Vas": 0.029188729770327368
      },
      "box": { "BType": 0, "Vr": 0.02, "Qlr": 10, "Qar": 100, "Qpr": 100 },
      "environment": { "T": 293.15, "p": 101325, "phi": 0.3 },
      "signal": { "Rg": 0.1, "P": 1 }
    },
